 "findings": [
  "Tester vt[0x18] was called from exactly three return sites in both complete sessions: 18dda4b (18dd400 direct path), 18e0a02 (terrain wrapper 18e0980) and 18e0922 (terrain wrapper 18e08a0). Every call had capacity 500. Every tester call on a thread was preceded by the matching selector call (0 cell mismatches; 0 calls without a preceding selector).",
  "Only six kind pairs reached tester vt[0x18]: (2,4) and (4,4) on the direct path; (2,6) and (4,6) via 18e0980; (2,7) and (4,7) via 18e08a0. The selector also returned the (4,3) capsule x box tester, but only to the flagged-neighbor bodies (see below). No convex-hull (5) kind and no (2,2) pair was selected in 480 s of hooked riding, and no box pair reached vt[0x18].",
  "Direct path 18dd400 (return 18dda4b): max n = 1 in 30,376 calls ((4,4) 30,201 calls, max 1; (2,4) 175 calls, max 1). No n > 4 was observed on that path, so these sessions show no live overrun of the 198fdc0 payload rows. Box and hull testers never ran on that path, so their counts there remain unobserved.",
  "Terrain wrapper 18e0980 (kind 6): (4,6) max n = 12 (np-03; 11 calls with n > 4: n = 5,5,5,5,5,5,6,8,10,10,12), (2,6) max n = 2. Terrain wrapper 18e08a0 (kind 7): (4,7) max n = 4, (2,7) max n = 3. These counts go to 198f910, which reduces groups to four, not straight to 198fdc0.",
  "The flagged-neighbor bodies (selector returns 18dffd4 and 18e064b) selected only the (4,3) cell (289,079 + 254 = 289,333 selections) and never called tester vt[0x18]. In straight-line code after both returns, rcx = the selected tester and the code calls its slot +8 and tests al (calls at 18e011a and 18e0784). Slot +8 was not hooked, so those results are not observed.",
  "Bit 15 of a shape +0x28 word was set on at least one of the two shapes in every selector call (2,512,847 of 2,512,847); the plugin did not record which side.",
  "The n = 10/12 events in np-03 fell 3.3-3.4 s after the start of a 700 ms jump hold (at about 137 s); whether that was the landing is not established (no airborne flag was polled at that moment)."
 ],
 "limits": [
  "Two complete sessions, 240 s each, one start location (director spawn) and one descent line; the input helper was slow (11-16 s per action), so maneuvers were sparse.",
  "No rock or tree contact was identified: no box or hull kind ever appeared, and no crash/KO occurred. Whether such obstacles use kinds 3/5 is not shown here.",
  "Jump/landing alignment is by wall-clock bins (500 ms, offset uncertainty about 0.25 s); airborne state was not recorded at plugin resolution.",
  "Tester slot +8 (used by the flagged-neighbor bodies) was not hooked: its arity is unestablished, and a forwarding detour with a guessed arity could drop stack arguments.",
  "The coordinator source hash is that of the np-03 version; np-02 used the earlier action cycle described in driving_cycles.np-02 (the only change).",
